                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Bun
                    %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\bigg(Ind
                  \\Big(
                  \\mathcal{O}Mod
                  \\big(
                  Loc_{{}^L G}(\Sigma)
                  \\big)
                  \\Big)
                  \\bigg)_{Nilp_{Glob}}
                  \\overset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\mathcal{D} Mod\big(
                  Bun_G(\Sigma)
                  \\big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#ArinkinGaitsgory12"}> Arinkin &amp; Gaitsgory 12, conjecture 0.1.6
            ).
          %p
            This form is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+geometric+Langlands+conjecture"} categorical geometric Langlands conjecture
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GaitsgoryGLCWebpage"} Gaitsgory et al. 2025
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-modules"} D-modules
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks+of+G-principal+bundles"} moduli stacks of G-principal bundles
            play a central role in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            (in particular as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connections"} Hitchin connections
            on bundles of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographically
            dual to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+conformal+field+theory"} 2d conformal field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+dual+group"} Langlands dual group
            also appears in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric-magnetic+duality"} electric-magnetic duality
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "S-duality#Atiyah77"} Atiyah 77
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
            in general and in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            in particular. One proposal for a realization of the correspondence as an incarnation of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mirror+symmetry"} mirror symmetry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            is due to (
            %a{:href => "#KapustinWitten06"}> Kapustin &amp; Witten 06
            ), which however has not been turned into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theorems"} theorems
            yet. Another proposal for realizing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Langlands+correspondence"} local
            correspondence via another incarnation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mirror+symmetry"} mirror symmetry
            is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GerasimovLebedevOblezin09"} Gerasimov, Lebedev &amp; Oblezin 09
          %p
            The geometric Langlands conjecture has been motivated from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theoretic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+correspondence"} Langlands correspondence
            via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
            and some educated guessing, but there is to date no formalization of this analogy that would allow to regard number-theoretic and the geometric correspondence as two special cases of one “global”
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+analytic+geometry"} global analytic geometry
            statement. Cautioning remarks on the accuracy of the analogy and on the rigour of the mirror-symmetric proposals may be found in (
            %a{:href => "#Langlands14"}> Langlands 14
            ). Some discussion of how to possibly start to go about making the analogy more systematic are at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion+and+idelic+structure"} differential cohesion and idelic structure
          %div
