                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Langlands+correspondence"} geometric Langlands correspondence
          %h3#RelationToTDuality Relation to T-duality
          %p
            In some cases the passage between a Lie group and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Langlands+dual+group"} Langlands dual group
            can be understood as a special case of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#DaenzerErp"} Daenzer-vanErp
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+class+field+theory"} geometric class field theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+Satake+equivalence"} geometric Satake equivalence
            %li
              %p
