          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+physics"}> duality in physics
            ,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electro-magnetic+duality"} electro-magnetic duality
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Montonen-Olive+duality"} Montonen-Olive duality
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seiberg+duality"} Seiberg duality
                %li
                  %p
                    %strong geometric Langlands correspondence
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"}> S-duality
                      ,
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kapustin-Witten+TQFT"} Kapustin-Witten TQFT
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+geometric+Langlands+correspondence"} quantum geometric Langlands correspondence
          %h2#references References
          %h3#ReferencesOriginal Original
          %p The conjecture goes back to
          %ul
            %li#BeilinsonDrinfeld9x
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Beilinson"}> Alexander Beilinson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Drinfeld"} Vladimir Drinfeld
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantization of the Hitchin system and Hecke eigensheaves
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://math.uchicago.edu/~drinfeld/langlands/QuantizationHitchin.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~mitya/langlands/hitchin/BD-hitchin.pdf"} other pdf link
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li#Laumon87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%A9rard+Laumon"}> Gérard Laumon
              , sections 5.3 and 4.3.3. of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Correspondance de Langlands géométrique pour les corps de fonctions
          %p Proof in the abelian case is due to
          %ul
            %li#Laumon85
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%A9rard+Laumon"}> Gérard Laumon
                ,
                %em Transformation de Fourier géométrique
                Preprint IHES/85/M/52 (1985)
            %li#Laumon96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%A9rard+Laumon"}> Gérard Laumon
                ,
                %em Transformation de Fourier généralisée
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9603004"}> arXiv:alg-geom/9603004
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%A9rard+Laumon"}> Gérard Laumon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Travaux de Frenkel, Gaitsgory et Vilonen sur la correspondance de Drinfeld-Langlands
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AG/0207078"} math.AG/0207078
            %li#Rothstein96
              %p
                M. Rothstein.
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sheaves with connection on abelian varieties
              %p
                %em Correction to: “Sheaves with connection on abelian varieties.” Duke Math. J., 87(1):205–211, 1997.
          %p Proof that the original version of the conjecture is false in general is due to
          %ul
            %li#Lafforgue09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Lafforgue"}> Vincent Lafforgue
              ,
              %em
                Quelques calculs reliés à la correspondance de Langlands géométrique pour
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℙ
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^1
                (version provisoire)
              2009 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.jussieu.fr/~vlafforg/"}> web
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://vlafforg.perso.math.cnrs.fr/geom.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The refined version of the conjecture stated in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+geometric+Langlands+conjecture"} categorical geometric Langlands conjecture
          %ul
            %li#GaitsgoryRozenblyum
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Gaitsgory"}> Dennis Gaitsgory
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nick+Rozenblyum"} Nick Rozenblyum
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Notes+on+geometric+Langlands"}> Notes on geometric Langlands
                  , (
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~gaitsgde/GL/"}> web
                  )
            %li#ArinkinGaitsgory12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dima+Arinkin"}> Dima Arinkin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dennis+Gaitsgory"} Dennis Gaitsgory
                %em Singular support of coherent sheaves, and the geometric Langlands conjecture
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6343"}> arXiv.1201.6343
                )
          %p
            Other comments on the relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} TQFT
            include
          %ul
            %li#Kapranov95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"}> Mikhail Kapranov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Analogies between the Langlands Correspondence and Topological Quantum Field Theory
              %em Functional Analysis on the Eve of the 21st Century
              Progress in Mathematics Volume 131/132, 1995, pp 119-151
          %p
            Comments on the development of the geometric duality by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Langlands"} Robert Langlands
            himself:
          %ul
            %li#Langlands13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Langlands"}> Robert Langlands
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Search for a Mathematically Satisfying Geometric Theory of Automorphic Forms
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://publications.ias.edu/rpl/paper/2578"} IAS page
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pfpzET8UkF4"} video
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://publications.ias.edu/sites/default/files/lecture_6.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Langlands14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Langlands"}> Robert Langlands
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Problems+in+the+theory+of+automorphic+forms+--+45+years+later"} Problems in the theory of automorphic forms – 45 years later
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.nottingham.ac.uk/personal/ibf/files/sc3.html"} Symmetries and correspondences in number theory, geometry, algebra, physics: intra-disciplinary trends
          %p Langlands’s doubts about or dissatifaction with the “geometric Langlands program” expressed in these talks (where he suggests that his name not be associated with the “geometric” part of the program) eventually led to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Langlands"}> Robert Langlands
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Об аналитическом виде геометрической теории автоморфных форм
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://publications.ias.edu/rpl/paper/2678"} ias:2678
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://publications.ias.edu/sites/default/files/iztvestiya_3.pdf"} pdf
          %p This in turn led to the reaction
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Frenkel"}> Edward Frenkel
              ,
              %em Is there an analytic theory of automorphic functions for complex algebraic curves?
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.08160"}> arXiv:1812.08160
              )
          %p
            See also the deformation to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+geometric+Langlands+correspondence"} quantum geometric Langlands correspondence
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mina+Aganagic"}> Mina Aganagic
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Frenkel"} Edward Frenkel
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Okounkov"} Andrei Okounkov
              %em
                Quantum
                = succeed "-Langlands" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.03146"}> arXiv:1701.03146
              )
          %p
            Proof of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+geometric+Langlands+conjecture"} categorical geometric Langlands conjecture
          %ul
            %li#GaitsgoryGLCWebpage
              %p
