          %h3#ReferencesInterpretationInStringTheory Interpretation in string theory
          %h4#global Global
          %p
            An interpretation of the global geometric Langlands correspondence as describing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+twist"} topologically twisted
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mirror+symmetry"} mirror symmetry
            on its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            to 2d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-model"}> A-model
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-model"}> B-model
            \-type) was given in
          %ul
            %li#KapustinWitten06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Kapustin"}> Anton Kapustin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                %em Electric-Magnetic Duality And The Geometric Langlands Program
                , Communications in number theory and physics, Volume 1, Number 1, 1–236 (2007) (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0604151"}> arXiv:hep-th/0604151
                )
            %li#FrenkelWitten07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Frenkel"}> Edward Frenkel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                %em Geometric Endoscopy and Mirror Symmetry
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0710.5939"}> arXiv:0710.5939
                )
            %li#Witten08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                %em Mirror Symmetry, Hitchin’s Equations, And Langlands Duality
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0802.0999"}> arXiv:0802.0999
                )
          %p
            and discussed in the bigger picture of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            arising as the conformal invariance of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            in
          %ul
            %li#Witten09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Geometric Langlands From Six Dimensions
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Celebration of the Mathematical Legacy of Raoul Bott
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0905.2720"} arXiv:0905.2720
          %p Reflections on the history (and possible future) of this insight are in
          %ul
            %li
              interview with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"} Hirosi Ooguri
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/notices/201505/rnoti-p491.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            An exposition of the relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electro-magnetic+duality"} electro-magnetic duality
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#Frenkel09"}> Frenkel 09
            ) and in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Frenkel"}> Edward Frenkel
                ,
                %em What Do Fermat’s Last Theorem and Electro-magnetic Duality Have in Common?
                KITP talk 2011 (
                %a{:href => "http://online.kitp.ucsb.edu/online/bblunch/frenkel/"}> web
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Frenkel"}> Edward Frenkel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Overview of the links between the Langlands program and 4D super Yang–Mills theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://online.kitp.ucsb.edu/online/duallang_m10/frenkel"} video page
                %a{:href => "http://online.kitp.ucsb.edu/online/duallang_m10/frenkel/pdf/Frenkel_LanglandsQFT_KITP.pdf"} pdf
          %p Further developments are surveyed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"}> David Ben-Zvi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loop+Groups%2C+Characters+and+Elliptic+Curves"} Loop Groups, Characters and Elliptic Curves
          %p Further discussion is also in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Tamas Hausel,
                %em Global topology of the Hitchin system
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1102.1717"}> arXiv:1102.1717
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://geom.epfl.ch/files/content/sites/geom/files/Calgary0312.pdf"} pdf slides
            %li
              %p
                Kevin Setter,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Topological quantum field theory and the geometric Langlands correspondence
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://resolver.caltech.edu/CaltechTHESIS:09192012-150137728"} web
          %p
            Discussion from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meng-Chwan+Tan"}> Meng-Chwan Tan
                ,
                %em M-Theoretic Derivations of 4d-2d Dualities: From a Geometric Langlands Duality for Surfaces, to the AGT Correspondence, to Integrable Systems
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.1977"}> arXiv:1301.1977
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meer+Ashwinkumar"}> Meer Ashwinkumar
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meng-Chwan+Tan"} Meng-Chwan Tan
                %em Unifying Lattice Models, Links and Quantum Geometric Langlands via Branes in String Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.01134"}> arXiv:1910.01134
                )
          %p
            A relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            (of the group manifolds!) is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#DaenzerErp
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calder+Daenzer"}> Calder Daenzer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+van+Erp"} Erik van Erp
              %em T-Duality for Langlands Dual Groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1211.0763"}> arXiv:1211.0763
              )
          %h4#local Local
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Langlands+correspondence"} local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/archimedean+field"} Archimedean
            Langlands duality for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whittaker+functions"} Whittaker functions
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mirror+symmetry"} mirror symmetry
            of a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-model"} A-model
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-model"} B-model
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#GerasimovLebedevOblezin09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Gerasimov"}> Anton Gerasimov
                , Dimitri Lebedev,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+Oblezin"} Sergey Oblezin
              %p
                %em Archimedean L-factors and Topological Field Theories I
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0906.1065"}> arXiv:0906.1065
                )
              %p
                %em Archimedean L-factors and Topological Field Theories II
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.2016"}> arXiv:0909.2016
                )
              %p
                %em Parabolic Whittaker Functions and Topological Field Theories I
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.2622"}> arXiv:1002.2622
                )
        .revisedby
          %p
